This repository contains two kinds of material, under different terms.
Please read the scope note before reusing anything.


================================================================
SCOPE
================================================================

1. NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENSE — Philips firmware and derived material
----------------------------------------------------------------

The firmware of the Philips PM5139 and its sister models is the work of
Philips (later Fluke). It is reproduced here as the object of study, for
interoperability, repair and documentation of instruments that have been
out of support for decades. No copyright in it is claimed, and none can
be granted by this license. It is not placed under the MIT terms below.

This reservation covers, at least:

  M27512_PM5139_V13.bin              original firmware image
  M27512_PM5139_V15.bin              original firmware image
  M27512_PM5139_V20.bin              modified firmware, derived from V1.5
  patch_ok.bin                       modified firmware, derived from V1.3
  PM5139_V13_disasm.asm              disassembly, derived from the firmware
  PM5139_V15_disasm.asm              disassembly, derived from the firmware
  PM5139_V13_annotated.asm           the same, with our annotations added
  PM5139_V15_annotated.asm           the same, with our annotations added
  PM5139_Diff_V13_V15.txt            instruction-level diff of both images
  PM5139_Simulator.html              embeds the complete V1.3 firmware
  D27C64-2_PM5139_SINUS11_V15.bin    contents of the factory SinePROM
  D27C64-2_PM5139_SINUS11_V15.HEX    the same, as Intel HEX
  X28C64_PM5139_V15.bin              contents of the factory arbitrary EEPROM
  X28C64_PM5139_V15.HEX              the same, as Intel HEX
  D310_image.bin                     the same image, as used by the emulator
  D310_image_synthetic.bin           an earlier synthetic stand-in for it

and, generally, any file in this repository that reproduces firmware
bytes, is mechanically derived from them, or depicts their contents.

Where our own work is mixed into such a file — the annotations in the
annotated listings, the corrected waveform in M27512_PM5139_V20.bin, the
computed curves in D310_image_V20.bin — only our contribution is offered
under the MIT terms below. The surrounding original material is not.

If you hold rights in the original firmware and object to it being
reproduced here, please open an issue and it will be removed.


2. COVERED BY THIS LICENSE — the reverse engineering work
----------------------------------------------------------------

Everything written for this project: the documentation (README.md,
PM5139_*.md, HANDOVER.md, BACKLOG.md, CLAUDE.md), the tools and
emulators (all .py and .js files, shell.html), the symbol tables and
annotations, the generated waveforms and the plots of them.


